  "environment": "macOS real native Node/SDK/RawNode/Raft Engine/SQLite/LTX/TLS with conditional in-memory object stores; four actual nodes, three voters and a dormant standby across two histories, one group per scan batch, two real committed commands and exactly two business callbacks. Three private aggregation/failure cases use typed status samples. No cellar_internal_tests.",
  "limitations": "Component qualification only. All 91 unique Rust cases across three binaries and all 13 focused checks pass at this source: 48 Raft library, 27 host and 16 directory cases. The three new private cases cover partial/failed scans, original sample age, changed populations, old sequence completions, wrong status identities, ordering/cardinality and deadline refusal; a complete empty attached set may report a real zero. The new four-node case verifies every node-wide count across two histories while sampling one group per batch, including the dormant node, without executing additional business callbacks. Profile-disabled hosts do not start this scanner. This focused run does not repeat the separate 231-case/19-check record at ec21635, whose full 42 snapshot and 19 membership cases retain their own pin, or the earlier all-88 public Node regression. Missing/old samples remain ineligible for any future controller until freshness is checked; load supplies no read, quorum, membership or transfer authority. Capacity is declared, not measured. Owned automatic repair, six-node no-business-traffic recovery and automatic balancing remain required. MR-11 remains IN_PROGRESS and MR-12 through MR-17 remain TODO. No physical S3, power-loss, real failure-zone, production performance/capacity, larger tier, federation or complete release qualification is claimed. Existing vendored warnings remain visible.",
